  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biochar Project for Circular Climate-resilient Agriculture in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to propose viable business models that will effectively facilitate the implementation and operation of the project, thus ensuring its long-term sustainability.GGGI will offer technical assistance for the preparation of an investment-grade biochar project in the designated states. They are;1) Conduct a landscape analysis for biochar production and utilization in Vietnam2) Conduct the feasibility assessment and design carbon financing models for a biochar project.3) Design the investment models for the biochar project4) Support the study tours of key stakeholders to facilitate the exchange of knowledge and experiences in related areas in Korea, which include the circular agriculture model, the Measurement Reporting and Verification (MRV) of GHG, and the development of the carbon market in the rice farming area.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to identify strategies for introducing biochar production and utilization to foster an environmentally friendly and competitive climate-resilient agriculture industry in Vietnam. It will conduct a feasibility assessment of developing a commercial-scale biochar production facility and aims to establish an innovative green financing model for biochar projects with the use of advanced technologies. This project also seeks to attract investments in biochar production and commercialization by engaging stakeholders such as government officials, technical experts, private investors, and rural communities.</narrative>
  </description>
